# TODO

## High Priority

### 1. Fix multi-image archive — DONE
~~CLI collects `imageArgs=()` but tail uses `${image//\//_}` (last image only).
Multiple `-i` produces broken archive. Should iterate all images or warn.~~
Fixed: archive name now includes all pulled images (e.g. `a+b.tar.gz`), tags
tmp keys are registry-qualified via `rawImageArg`, `repositories` keys use the
full image reference.

### 2. Token caching — DONE
~~`get_token` called per-layer inside loops. Token valid ~300s.
Cache once per image, reuse across layers.~~
Fixed: `registryToken` cached once per image in `refresh_token`, reused by
`fetch_blob`, refreshed once on 401, persistent 401 exits `EX_AUTH` (2).

### 3. Podman/Docker runtime support — DONE
~~Script required `docker` for dependency checks/loading and only used Docker commands.~~
Fixed: auto-detects container runtime for loading (`podman` preferred, then `docker`),
supports explicit selection via `--runtime` and `CONTAINER_RUNTIME`, and allows
download/archive flows without a runtime when using `--dry-run` or `--no-load`.

---

## Medium Priority

### 4. Parallel multi-image download — DONE
~~Download multiple images concurrently with `&` + `wait`.~~
Fixed: when multiple images are requested, per-image processing runs in parallel
background jobs with result aggregation in original argument order. Shared blob
downloads are serialized with per-digest locks to avoid races/corruption when
images share layers.

---

## Low Priority

### 5. Lock file — DONE
~~Prevent two instances writing to same dir simultaneously (flock).~~
Fixed: `flock -n` on `$dir/.docker_dn.lock`; second instance exits with
EX_USAGE.

### 6. Add to upstream CLI
Maybe it will become a usable wrapper to original scripts.
Add to original cli `docker image download` (or equivalent container-runtime integration).

### 7. Python rewrite
Bash script with complex logic (HTTP redirects, JSON parsing, state management).
Python would simplify significantly — better error handling, argparse, requests library.

